<title>NETHERLANDS: ING Barings maintains KPN as a Hold.</title>
<headline>ING Barings maintains KPN as a Hold.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Oct 10 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>KPN	    Post/Telecoms    59.60   ING Barings</p>
<p>COMMENT: The acquisition of TNT, if it proceeds, will change the risk profile of KPN, pushing the company into a highly competitive and more cyclical market. On KPN's assumption that consolidation will begin as early as 1997, ING raises earnings estimates. KPN shares trade at discount of 30 pct against Amsterdam average while dividend yield is 50-60 pct higher than average. However, since competitors trade at similar discount and given increased risk, hold recommendation is maintained.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS	pvs	P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	4.89		  12.2     2.60</p>
<p>    1996		   5.25		  11.4     2.82</p>
<p>    1997		   5.75    (5.73)    10.5     3.17</p>
<p>    1998		   6.30    (6.22)     9.5     3.43</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
